---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { reader } from '../lib/content';

const journal = (await reader.singletons.journal.read())!;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Story — Virtue Literacy Africa"
  description="Virtue Literacy Africa was founded on evidence — on the lived realities of Africa's informal settlements, and the conviction that bearing witness was not enough."
  currentPage="/about"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Our Story</span>
      <h1>Africa is a continent of extraordinary possibility.</h1>
      <p>Its people are creative, resilient, and deeply capable. The question we were built to answer is not whether its children have what it takes &mdash; they do. It is whether the world around them has what it takes to see them, equip them, and give them the platform they deserve. Too often, the honest answer has been no. Virtue Literacy Africa exists to change that.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 1 — THE GAP -->
  <section class="background-section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <span class="kicker">The gap we are closing</span>
      <h2>A gap of provision, not potential.</h2>
      <p>Across Africa's informal settlements, children are growing up in communities where access to books is rare, where libraries do not exist, where civic education is largely absent, and where the structures that should be investing in their futures have not yet reached them.</p>
      <p>This is not a gap of potential. It is a gap of provision &mdash; between what these children are capable of and what has been made available to them. Between the futures they could build and the tools they have been given to build with. Between the contribution they could make to their communities, their countries, and their continent, and the opportunity they have been afforded to make it.</p>
      <p>Closing that gap &mdash; at every level, through every means available &mdash; is what Virtue Literacy Africa is for.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 2 — WHAT WE WITNESSED -->
  <section class="background-section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <span class="kicker">What we witnessed</span>
      <h2>It began in Kibera.</h2>
      <p>Our documentation work began in Kibera. Working inside one of Africa's most densely populated informal settlements, we listened, recorded, and bore witness &mdash; to the realities of daily life, to the struggles and the strengths of a community that has never lacked for resilience, and to a generation of children whose stories deserved to be told.</p>
      <p>What we encountered made one thing undeniable: that books, knowledge, and civic empowerment are not luxuries for children in informal settlements. They are necessities. And their absence is not inevitable. It is addressable &mdash; and we had both the responsibility and the means to begin addressing it.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <span class="callout-label">The publication</span>
        <h3>A Place Called Kibera</h3>
        <p>The process produced <em>A Place Called Kibera</em> &mdash; a landmark publication that gave voice to a community too often spoken about rather than spoken with. But more than a book, the work produced a mandate.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 3 — OUR RESPONSE -->
  <section class="background-section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <span class="kicker">Our response</span>
      <h2>One response, at two levels.</h2>
      <p>We built Virtue Literacy Africa to respond at two levels &mdash; because the gap operates at two levels.</p>

      <div class="ps-grid" style="margin-top:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.5rem)">
        <div>
          <h3>On the ground</h3>
          <p>At the community level, we go directly to the children. We bring mobile libraries into informal settlements; run literacy, storytelling, and civic education events where children are heard, celebrated, and equipped; and publish books that reflect African realities and nurture values, courage, and active citizenship. We run AI Learning Fellowships that turn the most determined young people into community innovators &mdash; and through Mwangaza, our offline AI programme, we put early detection and care tools into the hands of the caregivers, health workers, and teachers who serve these communities every day.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>At the policy table</h3>
          <p>At the level of knowledge and policy, we built {journal.name} ({journal.acronym}). The insights generated at the grassroots &mdash; about what children in informal settlements actually need, about what works and what does not &mdash; deserve a rigorous scholarly home: a platform that carries them into the research community, into policy institutions, and into the conversations that shape Africa's future at scale.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        <span class="callout-label">One response, two scales</span>
        <p>The programmes and the journal are not separate endeavours. They are the same response, at different scales. One reaches the child. The other works to shape the world the child is growing into.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VISION & MISSION -->
  <section class="vm-section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Our Foundation</span>
      <div class="vm-grid">
        <div class="vm-cell">
          <span class="vm-label">Vision</span>
          <h3>An Africa where every child, regardless of where they were born, has access to books, knowledge, and the tools to shape their future.</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="vm-cell">
          <span class="vm-label">Mission</span>
          <p>To document Africa's informal settlement realities and respond with mobile libraries, literacy events, civic education, values-based books, AI learning fellowships, and rigorous academic research &mdash; nurturing children who are not only literate, but informed, empowered, and ready to lead.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TARGET BENEFICIARIES -->
  <section class="beneficiaries-section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Who We Serve</span>
      <h2>Target beneficiaries.</h2>
      <ul class="beneficiaries">
        <li>
          <span class="bn">01</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Children aged 5&ndash;17</h4>
            <p>Children in Nairobi's informal settlements — Phase 1 focuses on Kibera, Mathare, and Korogocho.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">02</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Young people aged 18&ndash;28</h4>
            <p>Particularly aspiring civic leaders and AI enthusiasts, targeted through the AI Learning Fellowships programme.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">03</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Caregivers, parents, and community teachers</h4>
            <p>Adults who support children's learning at home and in informal school settings, including as primary users of the Mwangaza AI tool.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">04</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Persons with disabilities</h4>
            <p>Including children and caregivers navigating accessibility barriers in education and reading materials.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">05</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Researchers, practitioners, and policymakers</h4>
            <p>African and Africanist scholars who publish through, and draw evidence from, {journal.name} ({journal.acronym}).</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1.2rem">Phase 1 focuses on Nairobi. Phase 2 and beyond aim to scale to other Kenyan counties and eventually across Africa.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- IMPLEMENTATION PHASES -->
  <section class="phases-section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Implementation Approach</span>
      <h2>A phased, scalable model.</h2>
      <table class="phases-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Phase</th>
            <th>Timeline</th>
            <th>Geography</th>
            <th>Key Deliverables</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Phase"><span class="phase-name">Phase 1<span>Foundation</span></span></td>
            <td data-label="Timeline">Year 1&ndash;2</td>
            <td data-label="Geography">3 Nairobi settlements: Kibera, Mathare, Korogocho</td>
            <td data-label="Key Deliverables">2 mobile library units; 2 new VLA books published; 3 civic education events; 1 AI fellowship cohort; Mwangaza AI pilot; {journal.acronym} inaugural issue</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Phase"><span class="phase-name">Phase 2<span>Scale</span></span></td>
            <td data-label="Timeline">Year 3&ndash;5</td>
            <td data-label="Geography">Additional Kenyan counties</td>
            <td data-label="Key Deliverables">Expanded mobile library fleet; fellowship programme growth; 4 additional VLA titles; Mwangaza AI v2 with multilingual support; {journal.acronym} indexed and biannual</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Phase"><span class="phase-name">Phase 3<span>Pan-African</span></span></td>
            <td data-label="Timeline">Year 5+</td>
            <td data-label="Geography">Pan-African</td>
            <td data-label="Key Deliverables">Continental AI curriculum partnership; multilingual book series; diaspora fellowship track; pan-African research network around the {journal.acronym}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 4 — WHAT WE ARE BUILDING -->
  <section class="background-section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <span class="kicker">What we are building</span>
      <h2>A solvable problem, being solved.</h2>
      <p>An Africa where every child, regardless of where they were born, has access to books, knowledge, and the tools to shape their future. An Africa where evidence from the ground informs the decisions made at the top. An Africa where the gap between potential and opportunity is not a permanent condition but a solvable problem &mdash; being solved, systematically, one community, one child, one piece of research at a time.</p>
      <p>That is the Africa Virtue Literacy Africa is working toward &mdash; across six pillars, through one ecosystem, and with the unshakeable conviction that every child deserves to be seen, equipped, and given the chance to lead.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.25rem)"><a href="/team" class="btn">Meet the team &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="act">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Be part of it.</h2>
      <div class="act-grid reveal">
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Partner with us</h3>
          <p>Financial sponsors, in-kind donors, institutional partners, and governance organisations.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/get-involved">See how to get involved &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Visit the journal</h3>
          <p>Read, cite, submit to, or partner with the African Journal of Governance, AI and Development.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/ajgad">Explore the {journal.acronym} &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Contact us</h3>
          <p>Questions, media enquiries, or just a conversation about what we are building.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/contact">Get in touch &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
